From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:21:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] superio/nuvoton/nct6687d: Let a board turn on the filter of a
 sensor

init_sensors() writes the source of each sensor with its bit 7 masked
off: that bit (FILTER_EN) makes the EC average the readings of the
sensor, and EC firmwares turn it on for the thermal diodes and PECI.
The Lenovo firmware of the NCT6686D in the ThinkCentre Tiny boards
loads 0xa0, 0x82 and 0x83 into SENSOR_CFG for PECI 0.0 and the diodes
TD0P and TD1P.

Add sensor_filter[], one per sensor, off by default, so that the
boards that set none program what they program today.

TEST=Built lenovo/m920x, whose devicetree sets it on four sensors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/superio/nuvoton/nct6687d/chip.h         | 2 ++
 src/superio/nuvoton/nct6687d/nct6687d_hwm.c | 3 ++-
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/superio/nuvoton/nct6687d/chip.h b/src/superio/nuvoton/nct6687d/chip.h
index 44e28b6d19..ef222644a4 100644
--- a/src/superio/nuvoton/nct6687d/chip.h
+++ b/src/superio/nuvoton/nct6687d/chip.h
@@ -332,6 +332,8 @@ struct nct6687d_fan_config {
 struct superio_nuvoton_nct6687d_config {
 	struct nct6687d_fan_config fans[MAX_NUM_FANS];
 	enum nct6687d_sensor_src_select sensors[MAX_NUM_SENSORS];
+	/* Average the readings of the sensor, as EC firmwares do for the diodes */
+	bool sensor_filter[MAX_NUM_SENSORS];
 
 	enum nct6687d_peci_speed peci_speed;
 
diff --git a/src/superio/nuvoton/nct6687d/nct6687d_hwm.c b/src/superio/nuvoton/nct6687d/nct6687d_hwm.c
index e7d80f493d..6001f38431 100644
--- a/src/superio/nuvoton/nct6687d/nct6687d_hwm.c
+++ b/src/superio/nuvoton/nct6687d/nct6687d_hwm.c
@@ -220,7 +220,8 @@ static void init_sensors(const struct superio_nuvoton_nct6687d_config *conf)
 	hwm_reg_set_bits(HWM_CONFIG_REG, HWM_EN);
 
 	for (i = 0; i < MAX_NUM_SENSORS; i++) {
-		hwm_reg_write(SENSOR_CFG_REG(i), sensors[i] & SENSOR_SRC_SEL_MASK);
+		hwm_reg_write(SENSOR_CFG_REG(i), (sensors[i] & SENSOR_SRC_SEL_MASK) |
+			      (conf->sensor_filter[i] ? FILTER_EN : 0));
 
 		if (sensors[i] >= PECI_AGENT0_DOMAIN0 &&
 		    sensors[i] <= PECI_AGENT3_DOMAIN1) {
-- 
